# Fraud Transaction Pattern Analyser

A full-stack fraud detection system for digital payments that combines a transparent, rule-based risk-scoring engine with a trained Random Forest classifier — built with Flask, MySQL, and scikit-learn.

## Overview

This project analyses digital payment transactions in real time and flags suspicious activity using two complementary layers:

1. **Rule-based risk scorer** — an explainable, weighted scoring engine that evaluates each transaction across 8 factors (location, transaction amount, deviation from user's average spend, velocity, failed login attempts, device recognition, time of day, account age) and produces a 0–100 risk score.
2. **ML fraud classifier** — a Random Forest model trained on 14 engineered features to predict fraud probability, giving a second, pattern-based signal alongside the rule engine.

Transactions are automatically tiered into **LOW / MEDIUM / HIGH / CRITICAL** risk levels, each triggering a different recommended action (approve, review, hold & verify, or block) and a corresponding SMS/email alert.

## Features

- 🔐 **User authentication** — registration and login with hashed passwords (Werkzeug), role-based access (admin / analyst)
- 📊 **Live dashboard** — real-time stats, risk distribution charts, and fraud-vs-legitimate breakdown (Chart.js)
- 🧮 **Dual-layer risk engine** — rule-based scoring + ML classification running side by side
- 🚨 **Automated tiered alerts** — SMS and email templates that scale in urgency with risk level
- 📈 **Reports & analytics** — fraud breakdowns by merchant, location, hour of day, and payment method
- 👥 **Admin panel** — user management, login activity logs, per-analyst transaction stats
- 🔍 **Transaction explorer** — searchable, filterable, paginated transaction history with full detail view per transaction
- 🧪 **Interactive "Analyse" tool** — manually enter transaction details and get an instant risk score with a full factor breakdown

## Tech Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|---|---|
| Backend | Python, Flask |
| Database | MySQL |
| Machine Learning | scikit-learn (Random Forest), Pandas, NumPy |
| Frontend | HTML, CSS, JavaScript, Chart.js, DataTables.js |
| Auth | Werkzeug (password hashing) |

## Project Structure

```
fraud_analyser/
├── app.py                     # Flask routes & app entry point
├── config.py                  # App configuration
├── database.py                # MySQL connection & queries
├── run_risk_alerts.py         # Batch scoring + alert generation pipeline
├── data/
│   ├── generate_data.py       # Synthetic transaction data generator
│   └── transactions.csv       # Sample transaction dataset
├── models/
│   ├── train_model.py         # Trains and evaluates the Random Forest model
│   └── fraud_model.pkl        # Saved trained model
├── modules/
│   ├── risk_scorer.py         # Rule-based risk scoring engine
│   ├── fraud_detector.py      # ML model inference (single + batch)
│   ├── feature_engineering.py # Feature transforms for the ML model
│   └── alert_system.py        # SMS/email alert generation
├── templates/                 # Jinja2 HTML templates
└── static/                    # CSS/JS assets
```

## How the Risk Score Works

Each transaction is scored out of 100 across 8 weighted factors:

| Factor | Weight |
|---|---|
| Amount deviation from user average | 20 |
| Location risk (domestic / international / unknown) | 17 |
| Transaction velocity | 18 |
| Failed login attempts | 15 |
| Absolute transaction amount | 10 |
| Unrecognised device | 8 |
| Unusual hour of day | 7 |
| New account age | 5 |

Scores map to risk levels:

| Score | Level | Action |
|---|---|---|
| 0–29 | LOW | Approve |
| 30–59 | MEDIUM | Review |
| 60–79 | HIGH | Hold & Verify |
| 80–100 | CRITICAL | Block |

## Machine Learning Model

- **Algorithm:** Random Forest Classifier (`n_estimators=100`, `max_depth=10`, `class_weight="balanced"`)
- **Features:** 14 engineered features including amount deviation, velocity, failed attempts, account age, and derived binary risk flags
- **Dataset:** 10,000 synthetically generated transactions (8.2% fraud rate) — see `data/generate_data.py`

> **Note on the dataset:** Transactions are synthetically generated with fraud/legitimate patterns constructed from the same feature logic used in training, so the trained model achieves very high evaluation scores on this sample data. This is expected for a demo/synthetic dataset and is documented here for transparency — in a production setting, the model would need to be retrained and validated on real, independently-labeled transaction data.

## Getting Started

### Prerequisites
- Python 3.9+
- MySQL Server

### Installation

```bash
git clone https://github.com/LikhithaMalgireddy/fraud-transaction-analyser.git
cd fraud-transaction-analyser
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

Update your database credentials in `config.py`, then:

```bash
# Generate sample data
python data/generate_data.py

# Train the fraud detection model
python models/train_model.py

# Run the batch risk-scoring + alert pipeline (optional)
python run_risk_alerts.py

# Start the web app
python app.py
```

The app will be available at `http://localhost:5000`.

## Future Improvements

- Retrain on real-world or independently-labeled transaction data for production-grade accuracy metrics
